{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794256575061,"sessionID":"ses_e3e029769ffeisrMdx9MsUggdV","part":{"id":"prt_1c2069a3e001sSmLgJWGrrx4IF","messageID":"msg_1c2067525001PsO5o69e5cHM0D","sessionID":"ses_e3e029769ffeisrMdx9MsUggdV","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794256575062,"sessionID":"ses_e3e029769ffeisrMdx9MsUggdV","part":{"id":"prt_1c2069a40001ETC5N1xXLzwFh5","messageID":"msg_1c2067525001PsO5o69e5cHM0D","sessionID":"ses_e3e029769ffeisrMdx9MsUggdV","type":"text","text":"The URL shortener is built: the Flask API and SQLite storage are in `backend/app.py`, and the React/Tailwind frontend is in `frontend/src/App.tsx` and `frontend/src/api.ts`. Docker isn't available in this sandbox, so I haven't built or run the image. I ran the app locally with gunicorn instead: a curl script over the main API flows gave the expected status codes, and the frontend type-checks and builds. I didn't click through the frontend in a browser.\n\n**What the curl tests confirmed:**\n- Register, sign in and sign out work. Wrong credentials, a missing token or someone else's link get 401 or 403.\n- Shortening accepts only `http`/`https` addresses and returns `short_code` and `short_url`.\n- The public list is newest first with paging.\n- `/r/<code>` answers 302 to the original address and adds one click. Unknown or disabled codes get 404.\n- Disabled links drop out of the public list and their endpoints answer 404, but the admin still sees them and can re-enable them.\n- When `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is unset or empty, admin sign-in is refused and existing admin tokens stop working. Data in `./data` survived a restart.\n\n**Choices the spec didn't settle:**\n- I changed the Dockerfile's pip step. The original command (install `requirements.txt` with the lock as constraints) failed here because the lock file has hashes. It now installs straight from `backend/requirements.lock` with `--require-hashes`. I also set gunicorn to 2 workers with 4 threads.\n- Sign-in tokens are random, stored only as SHA-256 hashes, and expire after 30 days.\n- Usernames must be 3–64 characters from letters, digits and `_ . @ + -`, and passwords at least 4 characters. Nobody can register the name `admin`. A taken username gets 409.\n- Links carry an extra `is_active` field.\n- I added three endpoints the spec didn't list: `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` for the frontend, and a JSON 404 for unknown `/api/*` paths.\n- A redirect sends the stored address exactly as given. Flask would normally rewrite it, for example lowercasing `HTTPS://Example.com`. Addresses with non-ASCII characters are encoded so they are valid in a header.\n\n**Other changes:** I added Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type packages at pinned versions, plus an `npm run typecheck` script. I also added a `.gitignore` and extra `.dockerignore` entries.","time":{"start":1794256575040,"end":1794256575043}}}
